  "summary": "Labour's Sadiq Khan was re-elected for a historic third term as Mayor of London, the first mayoral contest held under first-past-the-post after the Elections Act 2022 abolished the Supplementary Vote. Khan took 44% of the vote, comfortably ahead of Conservative Susan Hall on 33%. Labour remained the largest group on the London Assembly with 11 of the 25 seats, winning a record 10 of the 14 constituencies. The Liberal Democrats took the South West constituency — the first Assembly constituency ever won by a party other than Labour or the Conservatives — and Reform UK won its first London-wide seat.",
  "highlights": [
    "Sadiq Khan wins a record third term as Mayor of London",
    "First mayoral election held under first-past-the-post (replacing the Supplementary Vote)",
    "Labour wins 10 of 14 constituencies — the most any party has won since 2000",
    "Lib Dems take South West — first constituency won by neither Labour nor the Conservatives",
    "Reform UK wins its first London Assembly seat",
    "Turnout 40.5%, marginally down from 40.9% in 2021"
